02:30.739 --> 02:34.155
SHINING IN THE STORM

02:36.905 --> 02:39.697
This looks like it's going to be an awesome end!

02:41.405 --> 02:43.405
The final battle!

02:43.405 --> 02:44.780
Um... Yeah.

02:44.780 --> 02:50.155
It'll have a ton of CG compositing,
and the script is the best!

02:50.155 --> 02:51.447
Yagami...

02:52.614 --> 02:55.822
Is something wrong? You just seem...

02:56.155 --> 02:58.947
It's like you're trying to hard to be upbeat.

02:58.947 --> 03:00.864
Not at all!

03:03.447 --> 03:06.697
You've been editing the
making-of video on your PC.

03:06.697 --> 03:11.489
Oh, yeah. It's still pretty much
a rough cut at the moment.

03:15.530 --> 03:19.072
It... It's not what you think!

03:15.531 --> 03:19.072
We were packed in like sardines that day!

03:24.447 --> 03:26.614
It was fun, wasn't it?

03:26.739 --> 03:30.197
I wonder if I'll ever be
fired up like that again.

03:30.322 --> 03:31.822
Yagami...

03:32.614 --> 03:34.530
Say...

03:34.530 --> 03:38.405
Isn't there anything left for us to do?

03:38.780 --> 03:42.530
We finished Cos-Prayers for a DVD release,

03:42.530 --> 03:47.322
so it's not like the people who
supported us on TV won't see it.

03:48.405 --> 03:53.364
But I have this sad feeling, like I
don't want to say goodbye to Koto.

03:53.614 --> 03:55.030
Yagami...

03:58.697 --> 03:59.947
You're right.

04:02.447 --> 04:07.405
Takahara-sensei was the one
who cleaned up my amateurish script.

04:07.822 --> 04:12.530
And Kurume was the one working
behind the scenes to restart production.

04:14.822 --> 04:17.614
In the end,
I wasn't able to do anything.

04:18.114 --> 04:20.405
I was just along for the ride.

04:21.864 --> 04:23.655
So, let's go find it.

04:24.197 --> 04:26.280
Find what we can do for this!

04:26.280 --> 04:28.280
Ooizumi...

04:29.155 --> 04:30.405
Right!

04:31.739 --> 04:34.655
We'd like to put out a message that
we'd like the broadcast to resume.

04:35.447 --> 04:37.822
From Yagami and all of us,
just speaking straight.

04:38.155 --> 04:41.947
We'd really like to say something
to all the people who have supported us!

04:41.947 --> 04:43.947
IWASAKI AESTHETIC SALON

04:44.572 --> 04:47.239
I know how you feel, and I'd like to help, but...

04:48.697 --> 04:50.739
I think it would be difficult.

04:51.572 --> 04:55.864
Broadcasting a personal message
video would just be...

04:56.114 --> 04:57.364
Yeah.

04:57.364 --> 04:59.530
Really?

04:59.530 --> 05:00.739
Yes.

05:14.447 --> 05:16.364
They said no.

05:16.655 --> 05:22.030
EVENT SHOW

05:16.989 --> 05:20.072
Ikita pushed really hard for it, too.

05:20.072 --> 05:23.864
Same, here. My boss called in
every connection she had, but...

05:24.989 --> 05:26.447
I see.

05:28.197 --> 05:30.572
PERFORMANCE CANCELED

05:28.198 --> 05:30.572
Due to circumstances beyond our control,
the Super Transforming Cosplayers
live event has been canceled.

05:28.202 --> 05:30.572
We apologize for any inconvenience.
- The Management

05:31.905 --> 05:34.155
Hey, Mom?

05:34.697 --> 05:39.447
Why aren't the Cos-Prayers coming?

05:34.698 --> 05:39.447
Did they get lost?

05:39.739 --> 05:41.030
We...

05:42.989 --> 05:45.989
Isn't there anything we can do?

05:51.530 --> 05:53.280
Maybe...

05:53.280 --> 05:55.947
Maybe we can get the event reopened.

05:57.114 --> 06:00.322
We'll put out the word to the show's
supporters on the Net or something.

06:00.739 --> 06:04.739
Maybe, if we get everyone to gather here,
something will get started.

06:05.114 --> 06:07.572
Get everyone...

06:08.822 --> 06:11.114
You're right.

06:11.697 --> 06:16.197
Get everyone's feelings to be as one,
like what Miko-Rayer would do!

06:23.489 --> 06:26.989
To everyone who's supported
Super Transforming Cosplayers,

06:27.072 --> 06:30.864
will you add your voices to call for its renewal?

06:31.030 --> 06:33.322
We'll be waiting for everyone...

06:33.322 --> 06:36.739
at the Nogai Stage in Shiba Park near
Tokyo Tower at noon in one week.

06:36.739 --> 06:38.364
We want the
feelings of everyone...

06:38.364 --> 06:40.864
who wants the show renewed
to come together as one!

07:14.447 --> 07:15.905
I guess...

07:16.114 --> 07:17.447
Yagami!

07:17.447 --> 07:19.322
It's no use.

07:20.280 --> 07:23.447
No one came.

07:24.489 --> 07:26.072
I guess...

07:30.155 --> 07:30.989
Yagami!

07:35.405 --> 07:36.530
Yagami!

07:36.530 --> 07:37.989
Ooizumi...

07:37.989 --> 07:41.739
I'll always keep on rooting for you!

07:41.905 --> 07:44.280
No matter how busy or tired I am,

07:44.280 --> 07:46.447
or if I you can only be with me
on the TV or in photos!

07:46.989 --> 07:49.780
Even if I was the
last person on Earth,

07:49.780 --> 07:51.780
I'll keep rooting for you!

07:52.614 --> 07:54.822
Because... Because I love you!

07:55.280 --> 07:58.697
So... Right now, sing! Even if it's just for me!

07:58.864 --> 08:01.739
And hope that it reaches
everyone who isn't here!

08:13.322 --> 08:15.155
Ikita! Tanigawa!

08:16.072 --> 08:17.739
Senpai?

08:18.739 --> 08:21.280
Hayakawa okayed this, right?

08:21.447 --> 08:23.197
Yeah, pretty much.

08:23.447 --> 08:26.114
Just on condition that I accept
responsibility for it.

08:26.697 --> 08:29.364
Responsibility...? Senpai?!

08:29.364 --> 08:30.614
Let's go, Yayoi!

08:30.614 --> 08:31.989
Oh! Wait for me!

08:33.072 --> 08:37.322
Underneath this sky

08:39.780 --> 08:44.780
Feeling so small and weak

08:46.364 --> 08:52.239
Feeling like there's nothing you can do

08:52.947 --> 08:56.780
With your eyes cast down

08:59.739 --> 09:04.030
At a time like that, there will be

09:06.405 --> 09:11.614
A person who stays at your side

09:13.114 --> 09:18.697
You'll feel a reassuring warmth

09:19.822 --> 09:22.947
And then open up your eyes

09:26.489 --> 09:30.697
Why is it that you're here?

09:33.072 --> 09:36.947
It's because you're alive

09:39.822 --> 09:46.322
Take your hand and theirs

09:46.322 --> 09:53.405
And put them together

09:56.072 --> 09:58.864
You're not alone

09:58.947 --> 10:02.239
Everyone is here with you

10:02.697 --> 10:08.905
If you put your wishes into the song you sing

10:09.322 --> 10:15.655
Bring a smile to all the world

10:16.030 --> 10:22.030
And a rainbow bridge will appear

10:22.697 --> 10:26.030
You're not alone

10:26.030 --> 10:29.405
Everyone is here with you

10:29.405 --> 10:35.989
If you put your wishes into the song you sing

10:35.989 --> 10:42.322
Bring a smile to all the world

10:42.322 --> 10:42.947
Everyone...

10:42.323 --> 10:42.947
Bring a smile to all the world

10:42.947 --> 10:43.614
Everyone...

10:42.948 --> 10:52.308
Do you see the rainbow bridge in the sky?

11:04.739 --> 11:08.405
Yeah... This is it. This is it!

12:59.322 --> 13:03.989
In the end, they finally let me
rewrite the script as I wanted to.

13:04.072 --> 13:06.697
The show's last scene was reshot.

13:07.530 --> 13:10.155
And it's not just going
to be a DVD release.

13:11.030 --> 13:13.864
They're going to be
broadcasting it on TV.

13:14.447 --> 13:18.739
That's right. Our voices moved the world.

13:18.739 --> 13:21.739
They've decided to renew
the show, starting in December.

13:22.280 --> 13:26.197
Could you ask for a better plot twist?

13:22.281 --> 13:26.197
A happy ending!

13:49.489 --> 13:52.030
It's not what you think, Yagami! Just now-

13:52.030 --> 13:53.989
What are you looking at?!

13:55.864 --> 13:59.947
Ooizumi... Ooizumi...

14:00.322 --> 14:01.905
YOU IDIOT!

14:01.905 --> 14:06.614
But it looks like I still have a ways
to go to get MY happy ending.

14:06.864 --> 14:08.822
THE END
